Optional mask-aware FlashAttention-3 extension

This extension combines project Python/C++/CUDA integration with separately
licensed FlashAttention Hopper and NVIDIA CUTLASS/CuTe source. The repository's
Apache-2.0 grant for project integration does not replace the BSD-3-Clause
licenses and original copyright notices on those dependencies.

FlashAttention Hopper
--------------------
Upstream: https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention
Comparison reference: v2.8.3, commit
060c9188beec3a8b62b33a3bfa6d5d2d44975fab.
Reference source: https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/tree/060c9188beec3a8b62b33a3bfa6d5d2d44975fab/hopper

The 33 bundled Hopper headers are a modified source subset. All have matching
paths in that comparison reference: 18 are byte-identical and 15 differ.
This comparison identifies an upstream reference; it does not establish that
the supplied snapshot was copied from exactly that tag or commit.
Project changes include packed boolean-mask parameters, mask application and
tile/row metadata, launch and scheduling adaptations, and SM90 specialization.
Existing author notices remain on the bundled files, including Tri Dao and
Jay Shah, Ganesh Bikshandi, Ying Zhang, Vijay Thakkar and Pradeep Ramani.

The bundled LICENSE is byte-identical to the upstream BSD-3-Clause LICENSE
at the comparison reference. Its referenced AUTHORS file is supplied from
that same reference in vendor/flash_attn_hopper/AUTHORS. See
vendor/flash_attn_hopper/LICENSE for the governing terms. Preserve those
terms and attribution when distributing source or a compiled extension.

